#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176049 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175695 :question/id #uuid "2f4571af-99cf-5a4a-9998-fb6a0f7d6be9" :question/math-academy-id "e-11004" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\tan x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The zeros of the function are at $x = \\pi n.$\n\n- The function has asymptotes at $x = 2\\pi n.$\n\n- The range of the function is $y\\in [-1,1].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\tan x.$\n\n![](images/32/326418398ce1a33f03a21f3bdb58107856f4ccb72241429f1604486281e60822.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The zeros occur at $x=0, \\pm \\pi, \\pm2\\pi,\\ldots,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function has an asymptote at $x = \\dfrac \\pi 2$ and the period is $\\pi.$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x = \\dfrac \\pi 2 + \\pi n.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function takes values on all the real numbers, hence the range is $y\\in (-\\infty, \\infty).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049155 :topic/math-academy-id 1493 :topic/title "Graphing Tangent and Cotangent"}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516015 :question-generator/id #uuid "2399ae82-84c3-57ba-bdd7-aa55a1ab3695" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186176049.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176452 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ba1a255-23c5-558c-890e-352eda666203" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438028} {:answer/id #uuid "81040fec-7087-5a36-951b-b14d732d3182" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438029}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ba1