ction has asymptotes at $x=n\\pi .$\n- **II.** The function returns only positive values on the intervals $(\\pi n,\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n)\\,.$\n- **III.** The function has zeros at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/32/326418398ce1a33f03a21f3bdb58107856f4ccb72241429f1604486281e60822.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has an asymptote at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function returns only positive values on the interval $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the function is positive on $(n\\pi ,\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi )\\,.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi .$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176453 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06caa996-019d-55b8-9b18-5c983270de02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439615} {:answer/id #uuid "f490172a-f960-5273-937b-4f942ee332ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f490172a-f960-5273-937b-4f942ee332ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439616} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed2f5e64-32f3-5522-8385-0836cdf1b1de" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440165} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c0e3f19-9827-5a02-9335-759832aa58f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439617} {:answer/id #uuid "25bf5a5c-a822-56a1-a1c2-c6a5ab56d691" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 175