ach statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm\\pi,\\pm2\\pi,\\ldots,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function has an asymptote at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ and the period is $\\pi.$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function takes values on all the real numbers, hence the range is $(-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516011 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a49c3a6-2c06-51bc-844d-138fc04973bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515932} {:answer/id #uuid "6522cf60-890d-55a8-a675-5cbeb35202f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a49c3a6-2c06-51bc-844d-138fc04973bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515932} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d5a7135-c828-5ac9-9f26-2582cf461adc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515967} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fe3f231-f5ba-5be1-be9e-5913a0ba515b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515918} {:answer/id #uuid "d6809d06-ba04-53eb-a13b-c80cbe50f533" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fe3f231-f5ba-5be1-be9e-5913a0ba515b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515918} :answer-field/id #uuid "d49fd3a5-9c47-585e-8b53-058417e9e66d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515990} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "887815d4-2bcf-5d8b-9e5f-f7ea52b630ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515957} {:answer/id #uuid "e1858030-90d1-596e-94f4-b3d56ccfa68e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "887815d4-2bcf-5d8b-9e5f-f7ea52b630ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515957} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbb88c09-f4d5-55b1-a3f8-9fd61d296e7d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516010}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fd8d12b3-aeb5-5b1d-8119-9c9bbba0e242" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\tan x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The domain is all real numbers except $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$\n- **II.** The function is positive throughout $(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi,n\\pi).$\n- **III.** The least positive period is $\\pi.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\tan x.$\n\n![](images/e6/e65a2728d8bdad40af736ced1ec8303bf10fb4d11fc66b33784663512093a26b.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function is defined everywhere except where $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function is positive on $(0,\\frac{\\pi}{2})$ and negative on $(-\\frac{\\pi}{2},0).$ The period is $\\pi,$ so these signs repeat after each integer multiple of $\\pi.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The graph repeats after a horizontal shift of $\\pi,$ and no smaller positive shift repeats the whole graph. Therefore, the least positive period is $\\pi.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516013 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73b37b97-b986-5456-8e62-34787bd79605" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 