4f49d006" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\tan x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The domain is all real numbers except $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$\n- **II.** The function is positive throughout $(n\\pi,\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi).$\n- **III.** The least positive period is $2\\pi.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\tan x.$\n\n![](images/e6/e65a2728d8bdad40af736ced1ec8303bf10fb4d11fc66b33784663512093a26b.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function is defined everywhere except where $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function is positive on $(0,\\frac{\\pi}{2})$ and negative on $(-\\frac{\\pi}{2},0).$ The period is $\\pi,$ so these signs repeat after each integer multiple of $\\pi.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The graph repeats after a horizontal shift of $\\pi,$ and no smaller positive shift repeats the whole graph. Therefore, the least positive period is $\\pi.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."}] :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"}]}
